Third-party content
-------------------

This distribution includes agent skills adapted from vendored third-party
material. Each adapted SKILL.md also carries a one-line provenance note, and
since 2026-07-29 a `license` field in its frontmatter naming the upstream.

Both exist because this file does not travel with a packaged skill. The
distribution unit is the skill directory, so anything at the repository root is
left behind by the installers, by `npx skills`, and by a `.skill` archive. The
body note is what a person reads; the frontmatter field is what a registry or a
packaging tool can inspect. Keep all three in agreement.

- repoprompt-workflows (RepoPrompt Workflows)
  - author: Balarama Bosch
  - license: MIT
  - upstream: https://github.com/moonray/repoprompt-workflows
  - adapted into: the Zen Agent Skills spec/verify spine skills, house-styled and
    portability-gated from their standalone SKILL.md sources. As each skill lands
    it is listed here. Current:
      - .agents/skills/spec-quality/SKILL.md
      - .agents/skills/spec-plan-readiness/SKILL.md
      - .agents/skills/test-quality/SKILL.md
      - .agents/skills/spec-conformance/SKILL.md

  - note: maintainability-review, when folded in, is doubly vendored. Upstream
    itself carries it from cursor/plugins ("thermo-nuclear" code-quality review
    lens, MIT, https://github.com/cursor/plugins). Record both provenances then.
